"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-19/omp-19/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/4/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/6e66a13a8fa112148a94c97b17706eed8dc1d73b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates via `int(amount * 100)`; `19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `1998`. Fix by converting through `Decimal` with explicit half-up rounding.\nThe bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, not in `totals.py`. `to_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, and `int()` drops everything after the decimal point. Because of how floats are stored, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026`, so it became `1998`. The same thing happened with `0.29 * 100` and `4.35 * 100`. Every test that passes a float price was coming out a cent short.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the amount through `str` to a `Decimal`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up to a whole cent. Going through `str` means the conversion uses the number as written (`19.99`), not the slightly-off float value.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed, and pip refused to install it here (the system Python blocks it), so I couldn't run the suite with pytest. Instead I imported the test modules and called each `test_*` function directly. All 4 tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the 1 in `tests/test_report.py` passed. I also spot-checked some edge cases:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `1.005` | `101` |\n| `-19.99` | `-1999` |\n| `0.1 + 0.2` | `30` |\n| `4.35` | `435` |\n\nTo confirm under pytest, run `python3 -m pytest tests` in an environment that has it.\n\n**Follow-up:** prices are still passed around as floats. A sturdier fix would be for `Line` to take `Decimal` or string prices directly, but that changes the API, so I didn't do it here.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 43428, "requests_cache_write": 34800, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2191736, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1822, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 6, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T03:24:37.014169+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.497, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.005, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1834, "tokens_cache_read": 43428, "tokens_cache_write": 34800, "tokens_fresh": 1834, "tokens_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_cache_read": 43428, "tokens_main_cache_write": 34800, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 1822, "tokens_output": 1822, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 43428, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 34800, "tokens_proxy_calls": 5, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_proxy_output": 1822, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 4, "ts_iso": "2026-10-12T20:24:37", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 5, "usage_raw": [{"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 14616, "cost": {"cacheRead": 0,